Part 5: Setup & Execution Instructions

1. Initialize the Project

Run the following commands in your terminal to initialize the Next.js app and
install all required dependencies:

npx create-next-app@latest ai-studio-clone --typescript --tailwind --app --eslint
cd ai-studio-clone
npm install @google/genai zustand lucide-react

2. Configure Environment Variables

Create a .env.local file in the root of your project:

GEMINI_API_KEY=your_actual_gemini_api_key_here

3. Launch Development Server

npm run dev

Open http://localhost:3000 in your browser. You will have a fully functioning
Google AI Studio with multimodal uploads, real-time token/cost telemetry, JSON
schema generation, and code export.
